// v0.2.9: the Guide. Pages are plain text (not printf formats); '\n' starts a paragraph.
CULT_STR(CULT_ACTION_GUIDE, "Guide")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_TITLE, "Guide")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_READ, "Read")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_TOPICS, "Topics")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_MORE_LATER, "More topics appear as the game opens up.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T1, "How reading becomes Qi")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T1_SUB, "What counts, and the weekly allowance")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T1_P1, "Only reading on this device counts, in CrossInk's EPUB and XTC readers. Plain .txt books record no reading time, so they earn nothing.\nTime on a page is counted when you turn to the next page. A page left open longer than the idle limit counts nothing at all, so a book left open overnight earns nothing. The limit is 5 minutes unless you change it in Settings > System > Reading Stats > Idle Time Threshold. Track Reading Stats must stay on.\nNothing is earned while the book is closed, and nothing is lost either. Reading done before this character was created never counts.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T1_P2, "Each minute read gives 10 Qi, times your Qi rate: talent, root purity, your Cultivation manual, grades and open meridian points. The Cultivator screen shows the rate.\nThe weekly allowance: full Qi for the first 14 hours read in a week (Monday to Sunday), half for the next 14, a quarter after that. It cuts Qi only. Spirit Stones, stamina, HP and age are never cut.\nReading also ages your cultivator: one year for every hour read.\nOpen the game after reading. The Return summary shows what the reading earned and what happened in those seasons.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T2, "Your first steps")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T2_SUB, "Body Tempering and Qi Condensation")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T2_P1, "In Body Tempering there is nothing to do but read. The nine layers fill one after another on their own. At Layer 9 with a full bar, choose Break through: the first breakthrough needs no key.\nMake sure the device's date and time are set. Daily tasks, the omen, your rival and the ranking need them.\nFinish books. Each finished book becomes a Technique Scroll. Equip a Cultivation manual for a faster Qi rate, and keep spare scrolls: from Qi Condensation on, every breakthrough needs one as a key.\nQi Condensation opens the first region to explore, alchemy, meridians, Daos and the ranking. A new cell on the Cultivator screen says (New!) until you open it.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T3, "Realms and breakthroughs")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T3_SUB, "Keys, chances, Great Perfection")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T3_P1, "Body Tempering and Qi Condensation have nine Layers; later realms have Early, Middle, Late and Peak. A full bar moves you up a stage by itself.\nAt the last stage a full bar is a bottleneck: choose Break through. From Qi Condensation on you need a key, an unequipped scroll of the right tier: Mortal into Foundation Establishment, Yellow into Core Formation, Earth into Nascent Soul, Heaven after that. A high Dao or a breakthrough pill can serve too. A scroll is spent only if you succeed.\nThe chance starts at 90, 70, 45 and 35% and drops 5 a realm after that. Dao Heart (full after 15 reading hours) adds up to 15. A failure costs a quarter of the bar and adds 15 to the next try.\nCore Formation and some later realms test you first with a Tribulation (lightning that costs HP) or a Heart Demon (three scenes).")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T3_P2, "From Qi Condensation on, a full bar at the last stage also offers Great Perfection instead of breaking through. Each half hour read there adds a point of consolidation, up to 40. It raises the next breakthrough chance by up to 15 and the grade you get on entering Foundation Establishment, Core Formation and Nascent Soul.\nA grade lasts the whole life. A good Foundation or Golden Core raises your Qi rate for good; a cracked one lowers it.\nWaiting at a full bar outside Great Perfection still earns depth, up to 20 points, which helps the same way but less.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T4, "HP, stamina and Spirit Stones")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T4_SUB, "How each refills, and being wounded")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T4_P1, "HP is lost in fights and to lightning. Reading heals 1 HP a minute. A quiet spot on the map heals half your HP, and tonics heal 20, 50 or 100%.\nBelow 30% of your max HP you are wounded: you fight 3 levels lower and are 15% less likely to slip away. Below 10% you are badly wounded: 6 levels lower and 30% less. The fight screen says so when it applies.\nA fight lost with your last HP is a collapse. You come to at the region's entrance with nothing taken from you, and the map stays closed until you have HP again.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T4_P2, "Stamina: 1 for every 6 minutes read, up to 20. Each step on a map costs 1, so a full bank refills in two hours of reading.\nSpirit Stones: 1 for every minute read plus 1 for every 2 pages, never more from pages than from minutes. Fights, ruins, caves and the ranking pay more. Merchants and travellers sell herbs, ores, tonics, talismans and recipe slips. Spare scrolls, pills and ingredients can be sold back.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T5, "Exploring")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T5_SUB, "Maps, danger, regrowth")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T5_P1, "From Qi Condensation each realm opens a new region: a 6 by 6 map under fog, entered from its edge. A step to a neighbouring tile costs 1 stamina, and you see what a tile holds once you stand on it: herbs, ores, ruins, caves, quiet spots, merchants, lairs, and the guardian on the far side.\nDanger is shown as a word, from Trivial to Impossible, comparing your level with the enemy's. Your level is 10 for each realm plus your stage, plus equipped Sword and Palm or Fist techniques and good grades.\nBandits can be paid off and spirits driven away with incense. From anything but a spirit you can try to slip away; a Movement technique makes it certain unless you are wounded.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T5_P2, "A lost fight costs HP and throws you back a tile. A beast or bandit you ran from may come back stronger, and a few enemies that beat you become nemeses.\nHerbs, ores, lairs and quiet spots grow back 3 reading hours after you use them. Merchants restock at the same time.\nChart every tile and beat the guardian to clear a region: a large reward, once. Twenty reading hours later the region reshapes into a new map with a new guardian, under fog again. A Region Talisman does it at once.\nCultivators also walk the roads. They may spar, challenge you, trade or talk, and they remember you.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T6, "Alchemy, meridians and Daos")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T6_SUB, "Pills, acupoints, reading habits")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T6_P1, "Alchemy: gather herbs and ores on the maps, then brew pills while you read. One brew at a time, finished by reading time. Recipes are different in every life. Learn them from recipe slips (prizes, merchants, beaten cultivators) or try two or three ingredients in an experiment.\nPills give extra Qi for a while, heal, add to a breakthrough chance or serve as its key, or raise your next grade.\nMeridians: from Qi Condensation each realm lets you open a few acupoints, each costing 5% of the realm's Qi. Every open point raises your Qi rate by 10%, and each channel adds a small effect of its own.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T6_P2, "Daos are hidden, each tied to a reading habit: reading every day, long sittings, long weekend reads, a favourite time of day, reading at all hours, finishing books.\nSlots open on entering Qi Condensation (two) and the next three realms (one each). An open slot takes the first Dao whose habit you show. After the fifth the path is settled for this life.\nEach Dao gains levels as the habit goes on and gives a small bonus, never to Qi. A Dao of high enough level opens a bottleneck by itself and is never spent.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T7, "Rival, ranking and nemeses")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T7_SUB, "Who you measure yourself against")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T7_P1, "Your rival is a cultivator of your own age who trains every day at a pace of their own. Read more and you pull ahead; read less and they lead. If you stop reading for a week they go into seclusion and wait. When one of you is more than a realm ahead, their pace changes until you are close again.\nOnce their realm has opened a region, one meeting on the road in four may be your rival. Sparring with them costs no HP. Their card shows how far ahead or behind they are.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T7_P2, "Each realm from Qi Condensation has a ranking of 20. Once a day you may challenge the place above you. A loss costs 10% of your max HP; a win pays Spirit Stones. Someone below may challenge you; declining costs nothing, and you never lose your place while away. The top three hold a title.\nNemeses: a beast, bandit or cultivator that beats you in a dangerous fight may remember you. It looks for you on the map, grows when it wins and comes back scarred when it loses. Its habits are hidden at first; fighting it, talking to travellers and listening to rumors reveal them.")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T8, "The Chronicle and the sleep screen")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T8_SUB, "Your life on record")
CULT_STR(CULT_GUIDE_T8_P1, "The Chronicle is your cultivator's life, written as you go: breakthroughs, fights, finds, rivals and the seasons in between. It opens at the newest page; its menu goes to the beginning or ten years at a time. Export a copy puts it in the Chronicles folder as a book you can read or share.\nTo see your cultivator whenever the reader sleeps, choose Cultivator or Cultivator (light) under Settings > Display > Sleep Screen. It shows your name, titles, realm and stage as of your last visit.\nNothing in the game decays while you are away. Reading is the only way forward, and stopping never costs you anything.")

